// Renode platform description for ATSAMD51P20 (Cortex-M4F).
//
// Renode upstream ships platforms/cpus/atsamd51g19a.repl but it's
// not usable for klipper SAMD51:
//
//   1. Memory layout is the G19 variant (512KB flash / 192KB SRAM);
//      klipper SAMD51P20 builds expect 1MB / 256KB.
//   2. It exposes only sercom3; klipper's host UART is SERCOM0
//      (PA10/PA11 - see src/atsamd/serial.c).
//   3. It models GCLK PCHCTRL[1] as a `flipflop.py` register, which
//      alternates 0/0xFFFFFFFF between reads. klipper's
//      enable_pclock() does `while (PCHCTRL[id].reg != val)` so the
//      flipflop never matches `val` and the firmware spins.
//
// We therefore stand the platform up from scratch rather than using
// the upstream as a base. OSCCTRL / GCLK / MCLK / OSC32KCTRL / CMCC
// stubs are runtime-injected by the launcher (Python.PythonPeripheral
// instances backed by samd_*_stub.py / samd_storeback.py) because
// their script paths are checkout-relative - same pattern AFEC uses
// on SAME70.
//
// IRQ 46 = SERCOM0_0 in the SAMD51 vector table. klipper installs
// the same SERCOM0_Handler on all 4 SERCOM0 IRQs (46..49), so wiring
// the SAMD5_UART model's single IRQ output to any of them is
// sufficient - the handler reads INTFLAG and dispatches RX/TX events
// regardless of which line raised the interrupt.

cpu0: CPU.CortexM @ sysbus
    cpuType: "cortex-m4f"
    nvic: nvic

nvic: IRQControllers.NVIC @ sysbus 0xE000E000
    -> cpu0@0

flash0: Memory.MappedMemory @ sysbus 0x0
    size: 0x100000

sram0: Memory.MappedMemory @ sysbus 0x20000000
    size: 0x40000

dwt: Miscellaneous.DWT @ sysbus 0xE0001000
    frequency: 120000000

sercom0: UART.SAMD5_UART @ sysbus 0x40003000
    ->nvic@46
